   "summary_zh": "订阅后可解锁这些内容 孟买已开始显现冬季的最初迹象。11月14日星期六（2026年），当地最低气温降至18.9摄氏度，而下午气温略有回升。尽管早晨仍相对凉爽，但预计下午气温将在29摄氏度左右徘徊，夜间随后降至22摄氏度。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Mumbai has started experiencing its first signs of winter, with the minimum temperature dipping to 18.9° Celsius, while the temperature rose slightly in the afternoon on Saturday (November 14, 2026). While mornings remained relatively cool, afternoon temperatures were expected to hover around 29° Celsius before dropping to 22° Celsius at night. According to the India Meteorological Department (IMD), the Santacruz weather station forecasts a minimum temperature of 19° Celsius and a maximum of 33° Celsius. From November 15 to 19, maximum temperatures are expected to remain around 33° Celsius before dipping slightly to 32° Celsius on November 20, marking warm afternoons. Meanwhile, Mumbai’s Air Quality Index (AQI) has shown signs of improvement after Diwali. On Saturday (November 14), the city’s AQI stood at 127, placing it in the ‘moderate’ category. However, several regions in Mumbai have recorded higher air pollution levels, with Nava Nagar recording an AQI of 200, Deonar at 178, and BKC at 183. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
