   "summary": "The SSG said the appointments underscored Governor Lawal’s commitment to inclusive and participatory governance, strengthening grassroots engagement, broadening citizens’ involvement in government affairs and enhancing effective communication of government policies, programmes and achievements across the state.",
   "summary_zh": "安全卫队表示，这些任命凸显了拉瓦尔州长对包容性和参与式治理的承诺，有助于加强基层互动、扩大公民参与政府事务的程度，并在全州范围内有效传达政府政策、方案和成果。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The appointments which took immediate effect were announced on Friday by the Secretary to the State Government, Malam Abubakar Mohammad Nakwada in a statement signed by Suleman Ahmad Tudu, the senior special assistant (media) in the office of the Secretary to the State Government. The SSG said the appointments underscored Governor Lawal’s commitment to inclusive and participatory governance, strengthening grassroots engagement, broadening citizens’ involvement in government affairs and enhancing effective communication of government policies, programmes and achievements across the state. He said the action further reinforced the administration’s commitment to accountability, transparency and people-centred development under the Rescue and Rebuild Agenda. The appointees according to him will assist the governor in a wide range of roles, including community engagement, grassroots mobilisation, matters relating to persons with disabilities, media & publicity and other duties as may be assigned. The government said the new aides are expected to serve as effective bridges between government and the people, ensuring that diverse community voices are heard and reflected in governance. Lawal charged the appointees to demonstrate dedication, loyalty, professionalism and commitment to public service. He urged them to see their appointments not as political reward, but as a call to serve, and to work to ensure that government policies reach every ward and community in the state. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
