   "title": "Midterm election results wouldn’t change India’s relationship with US: S Jaishankar at HTLS 2026",
   "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/midterm-election-results-wouldn-t-change-india-s-relationship-with-us-s-jaishankar-at-htls-2026-101794633951175.html",
   "domain": "hindustantimes.com",
   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Sat, 14 Nov 2026 11:01:42 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794634302.0,
   "ageDays": 0.15,
   "summary": "The midterm elections in the United States that delivered a setback for President Donald Trump and led to a victory of the Democrats in the US Congress would not change India’s relationship with the country, External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar said on Saturday. In the recently held midterm elections, the Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate from the Republicans.",
   "summary_zh": "印度外交部长S·贾伊尚卡尔周六表示，近期举行的美国中期选举使民主党在美国国会获胜，并给唐纳德·特朗普总统的共和党造成挫折，但这不会改变印度与美国的关系。在刚刚举行的中期选举中，民主党从共和党手中夺得了众议院和参议院的控制权。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The midterm elections in the United States that delivered a setback for President Donald Trump and led to a victory of the Democrats in the US Congress would not change India’s relationship with the country, External Affairs Minister S Jaishankar said on Saturday. Speaking with R Sukumar, Editor-in-Chief, Hindustan Times, at the 24th Hindustan Times Leadership Summit in New Delhi, Jaishankar said that there is consensus between India and the US on defence and security cooperation and other matters that are “not partisan\" in the United States. “In some cases, we will be focusing on the administration, for example, trade negotiations because it is their jurisdiction. To some extent, it would matter. To some extent, we would be continuing what we are doing,” he said. In the recently held midterm elections, the Democrats seized both the House of Representatives and the Senate from the Republicans. In the House of Representatives, the Democrats won 256 seats, while the Republicans won 169 seats, Associated Press reported. Meanwhile, the Democrats won 55 seats in the US Senate, leaving Republicans with 44 seats. The turbulence the world is going through could last a few years, maybe till the end of the decade, he said, adding that India's compass for navigating these choppy waters is the \"lens of national interest\". He touched upon the conflicts in West Asia and Ukraine, and also spoke of the crises parts of Africa are facing. Jaishankar spoke of a readjustment of the world order that includes the rise of new powers. The rivalry between the United States and China, he said, was one of the factors behind the ongoing frictions, but not the only one",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
