   "_dt": 1794633516.0,
   "ageDays": 0.16,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Federico Carò, a research scientist at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York, studies South Indian Buddhist sculptures and Gupta-period bronze-casting techniques. Science reveals aspects of art that are otherwise difficult to uncover. By investigating how artworks are made, for instance, scientific analysis encourages us to understand art not simply as the impulse of a royal or religious patron but also the work of an artisan.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅即可解锁这些内容。纽约大都会艺术博物馆的研究科学家费德里科·卡罗研究南印度佛教雕塑和笈多时期的青铜铸造技术。科学揭示了艺术中原本难以发现的层面。例如，通过研究艺术品是如何制作的，科学分析促使我们认识到，艺术不仅是国王或宗教赞助者的冲动体现，也蕴含工匠的劳动。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Federico Carò, a research scientist at the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York, studies South Indian Buddhist sculptures and Gupta-period bronze-casting techniques. Science reveals aspects of art that are otherwise difficult to uncover. By investigating how artworks are made, for instance, scientific analysis encourages us to understand art not simply as the impulse of a royal or religious patron but also the work of an artisan. It thus probes a range of humanistic concerns in the production, circulation, and preservation of art. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
