   "title": "PM Modi pays tribute to Jawaharlal Nehru on his 137th birth anniversary",
   "url": "https://www.hindustantimes.com/india-news/pm-modi-pays-tribute-to-jawaharlal-nehru-on-his-137th-birth-anniversary-101794628458414.html",
   "domain": "hindustantimes.com",
   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:20:46 +0530",
   "_dt": 1794631846.0,
   "ageDays": 0.18,
   "summary": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Saturday paid tribute to former Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru on his 137th birth anniversary, as the nation observes Children's Day in his memory. Defence Minister Rajnath Singh also paid tribute to the country's first Prime Minister, recalling his contribution to India's freedom struggle and his leadership during the formative years of independent India. After the death of Nehru, it was unanimously decided to celebrate his birthday as ' Bal Diwas ' or Children's Day in India.",
   "summary_zh": "印度总理纳伦德拉·莫迪于周六迎来前总理贾瓦哈拉尔·尼赫鲁诞辰137周年，并在这个国家纪念尼赫鲁的“儿童节”之际向其致敬。国防部长拉杰纳特·辛格也向这位印度首任总理致敬，回顾了他对印度独立事业的贡献以及他在独立初期印度的领导作用。尼赫鲁去世后，各方一致决定在印度庆祝他的生日，将其定为“儿童节”（Bal Diwas）。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Prime Minister Narendra Modi on Saturday paid tribute to former Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru on his 137th birth anniversary, as the nation observes Children's Day in his memory. Defence Minister Rajnath Singh also paid tribute to the country's first Prime Minister, recalling his contribution to India's freedom struggle and his leadership during the formative years of independent India. In a post on X, Singh said, \"On the birth anniversary of Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru Ji, I pay my tributes to him. His contribution to India’s freedom struggle and his leadership as the first Prime Minister of independent India left an enduring imprint on the formative years of our nation.\" November 14 is observed as Children's Day across the country to mark the birth anniversary of Jawaharlal Nehru, who was popularly known as 'Chacha Nehru' for his affection towards children. After the death of Nehru, it was unanimously decided to celebrate his birthday as ' Bal Diwas ' or Children's Day in India. Nehru was born on November 14, 1889, in Uttar Pradesh's Prayagraj . He breathed his last on May 27, 1964. He became the prime minister on August 15, 1947, following an active role in the freedom struggle of the country. On this day, a number of activities are organised for students in schools nationwide, such as games, competitions, and so on, while government bodies pay tribute to the late prime minister and organise commemorative events on this day. In 1954, the United Nations declared November 20 as Universal Children's Day and India used to celebrate Children's Day on that day before 1956, but after the death of Prime Minister Nehru in 1964, a resolution was passed in the Parliament unanimously declaring the day of Nehru's birth anniversary as National Children's Day",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
