   "title": "Oriire Abduction: Presidency Fires Back At Makinde, Says Tinubu Acted Swiftly",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/oriire-abduction-presidency-fires-back-at-makinde-says-tinubu-acted-swiftly/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:33:58 +0000",
   "_dt": 1794609238.0,
   "ageDays": 0.44,
   "summary": "His response followed Makinde’s disclosure during an interview that he did not speak with President Tinubu throughout the over 50 days the victims were held captive, despite attempts to reach the President through his aide. Addressing the governor directly, Ogra said the federal government remained focused on its mandate to secure and prosper Nigeria under President Tinubu.",
   "summary_zh": "他的回应紧随马金德披露的情况之后。马金德在采访中表示，在受害者被囚禁的50多天里，他始终没有与蒂努布总统说过话，尽管曾试图通过总统助理联系总统。奥格拉直接对州长表示，在蒂努布总统领导下，联邦政府仍专注于确保尼日利亚（国家，首都阿布贾）安全与繁荣这一使命。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Senior Special Assistant to the President on Digital and New Media, Otega Ogra, said the Federal Government immediately deployed military and intelligence assets to Oyo State following the incident. Ogra, in a post on his X handle, said the operations led to the successful rescue of all the abducted children and teachers on July 10, 2026. His response followed Makinde’s disclosure during an interview that he did not speak with President Tinubu throughout the over 50 days the victims were held captive, despite attempts to reach the President through his aide. Addressing the governor directly, Ogra said the federal government remained focused on its mandate to secure and prosper Nigeria under President Tinubu. He maintained that the President prioritised concrete action and results over political point-scoring in addressing security challenges. According to him, the administration has introduced measures to strengthen the country’s security architecture, including the creation of a new Homeland Security position, improved coordination under the Office of the National Security Adviser (ONSA), and better equipment and remuneration for the military. He added that the government had also improved welfare across the security and intelligence agencies. On Makinde’s comments regarding the Economic and Financial Crimes Commission (EFCC), Ogra stressed that the anti-graft agency remained independent and carried out its statutory responsibilities without political interference. He said President Tinubu had consistently maintained a non-interference policy regarding agencies and regulatory bodies with statutory independence. Ogra, however, criticised the governor’s comments, urging him to concentrate on governance and issue-based campaigning. “In my opinion, sir, political leaders like your good self should prioritise governance or focus on issues-based campaigning rather than such grandstanding that is now becoming the hallmark of your campaign,” he said. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
