   "summary": "Kim Jong-sik, first vice department director of the Central Committee of the ruling Workers' Party of Korea, made the remarks in a statement carried by the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA). He described nuclear submarine programs in South Korea, Japan and Australia as the \"detailed implementation\" of a new U.S. security strategy aimed at \"securing the maritime hegemony.\" \"This has become a root cause of seriously undermining the strategic balance in the region and sparking off a new arms race,\" he claimed.",
