   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Kim Jong-sik, first vice department director of the Central Committee of the ruling Workers' Party of Korea, made the remarks in a statement carried by the Korean Central News Agency (KCNA). \"Arms build-up of the U.S. and its vassal allies for seizing a maritime edge in the Asia-Pacific region has emerged as a new dangerous factor seriously disturbing regional peace and security,\" Kim said. He described nuclear submarine programs in South Korea, Japan and Australia as the \"detailed implementation\" of a new U.S. security strategy aimed at \"securing the maritime hegemony.\" \"This has become a root cause of seriously undermining the strategic balance in the region and sparking off a new arms race,\" he claimed. \"We will deter all threats by action and flexing of its bolstered muscle,\" he warned",
