   "title": "FM Cho to visit China this week for talks with Wang Yi on N. Korea, bilateral ties",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/others/20261112/fm-cho-to-visit-china-this-week-for-talks-with-wang-yi-on-n-korea-bilateral-ties",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:57:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1794495423.0,
   "ageDays": 1.76,
   "summary": "Foreign Minister Cho Hyun will visit China this week for talks with his Chinese counterpart, Wang Yi, on North Korea-related issues and bilateral relations, Seoul's foreign ministry said Thursday. Cho is scheduled to make a two-day visit to Beijing starting Friday, during which he will hold talks with Chinese Foreign Minister Wang and attend a dinner on the same day, according to the ministry. Cho's visit follows an invitation from Wang during their talks in Seoul in August.",
   "summary_zh": "首尔外交部周四表示，外交部长Cho Hyun将于本周访问中国，与中国外长Wang Yi就朝鲜相关问题和双边关系举行会谈。据该部消息，Cho定于周五起对北京进行为期两天的访问，期间将与中国外长Wang举行会谈，并于当晚参加晚宴。Cho此次访问是在8月双方于首尔会谈时，Wang向他发出邀请后安排的。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Foreign Minister Cho Hyun will visit China this week for talks with his Chinese counterpart, Wang Yi, on North Korea-related issues and bilateral relations, Seoul's foreign ministry said Thursday. Cho is scheduled to make a two-day visit to Beijing starting Friday, during which he will hold talks with Chinese Foreign Minister Wang and attend a dinner on the same day, according to the ministry. \"The two ministers plan to hold wide-ranging discussions on issues of mutual interest, including bilateral relations, developments on the Korean Peninsula and other regional issues,\" ministry spokesperson Park Doo-soon said at a press briefing. Cho's visit follows an invitation from Wang during their talks in Seoul in August. At the time, the two ministers exchanged views on bilateral relations and Korean Peninsula issues, with Cho calling for Beijing to play a constructive role in bringing North Korea back to dialogue. The visit will precede President Lee Jae Myung's planned trip to China to attend the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit in Shenzhen on Nov. 18-19. Chinese President Xi Jinping, U.S. President Donald Trump and other world leaders are also expected to attend the summit. The gathering is expected to provide an opportunity for Xi and Trump to meet. The possibility of a trilateral meeting involving Russian President Vladimir Putin on the sidelines of the summit has also drawn attention. There has also been speculation about a possible meeting between Trump and North Korean leader Kim Jong-un during Trump's trip to Asia, as the U.S. president has expressed interest in resuming dialogue with Pyongyang. \"While there have been various reports about the possibility of renewed U.S.-North Korea dialogue, we currently see little likelihood of any concrete moves. We are closely monitoring relevant developments,\" spokesperson Park said. \"We hope the resumption of U.S.-North Korea dialogue will help create a virtuous cycle of progress toward stability and peace on the Korean Peninsula,\" he added",
