   "summary": "Troops of the Nigerian Army have apprehended two suspected terrorists (father and son) in Sokoto State. The suspects, identified as Muhammadu Ali and his son, Umaru Ali, were arrested at Bauni Forest in Tangaza Local Government Area. The operational report made available to the News Agency of Nigeria (NAN) on Wednesday said the operation was conducted by troops of 248 Battalion, supported by the French Special Forces and the NCTC-Office of the National Security Adviser tactical team.",
   "summary_zh": "尼日利亚陆军部队已在索科托州逮捕两名疑似恐怖分子（父子二人）。据披露，两名嫌疑人为穆罕马杜·阿里及其子乌马鲁·阿里，他们在坦加扎地方政府辖区鲍尼森林被捕。尼日利亚通讯社（NAN）周三获得的行动报告称，此次行动由第248营部队实施，并得到法国特种部队及国家安全顾问全国反恐中心战术小组的支援。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Troops of the Nigerian Army have apprehended two suspected terrorists (father and son) in Sokoto State. The suspects, identified as Muhammadu Ali and his son, Umaru Ali, were arrested at Bauni Forest in Tangaza Local Government Area. The operational report made available to the News Agency of Nigeria (NAN) on Wednesday said the operation was conducted by troops of 248 Battalion, supported by the French Special Forces and the NCTC-Office of the National Security Adviser tactical team. The report said the suspects were apprehended at about 10:00 a.m. on Wednesday and were believed to be from the Bauni village area. According to the report, items recovered during the operation included one AK-47 rifle, one magazine containing three rounds of 7.62mm special ammunition, ₦9,760 and three motorcycle tubes. The report said the suspects were in the custody of 8 Military Intelligence Battalions for further investigation. (NAN) Comments expressed here do not reflect the opinions of Vanguard newspapers or any employee thereof",
